    "reading": {
        "body": "Samsung holds 108,943 of the tracked AI patents, more than the next two companies on the list, IBM at 69,827 and Apple at 31,794, combined.\n\nThe total patent count across 108 companies grew from 310,516 on August 14 to 312,470 by September 2, an increase of roughly 1,950 patents in under three weeks, moving in occasional jumps rather than a daily trickle. Beyond the top three, the list drops sharply: Huawei at 27,442 and Microsoft at 24,682 are the only other companies above 20,000, and by the time the list reaches Palantir at 1,668, the counts are two orders of magnitude below Samsung's.\n\nSeveral companies on this list also appear elsewhere on this site with product entries, Huawei's PanGu model, Tencent's Hunyuan, Xiaomi's MiMo, Baidu's ERNIE, and Alibaba Cloud's Qwen among them, meaning their patent volume sits alongside a specific named AI product rather than only an abstract filing count. Patent counts measure filing activity, not grant rates, litigation use, or which patents actually cover AI-specific inventions as opposed to a company's broader technology portfolio, so this data cannot support a claim about which company's AI research is more advanced.",
